  <title>Incoming invoices report</title>

  <p><guiseq><gui>Reports</gui><gui>Incoming invoices</gui></guiseq> lists the
  bills entered in <link xref="incoming_invoice"/>. Narrow it by
  <gui>Service provider</gui>, <gui>Expense account</gui>, <gui>Fiscal
  year</gui> and <gui>Paid with</gui>, or type into <gui>Search
  description</gui>. Select a bill to see its lines.</p>

  <p>The <gui>Paid with</gui> column shows how each bill was paid: by cheque
  (with its number), transfer, credit card or cash, and from which account. It
  is blank for bills entered before payments were recorded with them.</p>

  <p>Beside the list are how many bills are shown, the dates they span, how
  many service providers, and the smallest, largest, total and average
  amount.</p>

  <p>Right click a bill and choose <gui>View attachment</gui> to see its scan;
  if none is attached you can attach one, see <link xref="pdf_attachment"/>.
  <gui>Refresh</gui> is in the window menu.</p>

  <section id="edit">
  <title>Edit mode</title>
  <p>Check <gui>Edit mode</gui> in the window menu, which asks for the
  administrator password, to change descriptions in the list, to uncheck
  <gui>Reconciled</gui>, and to right click a bill and choose <gui>Edit
  incoming invoice</gui>; see <link xref="incoming_invoice_edit"/>.</p>
  </section>

</page>
